      "message": "fix(motion): circular ramp entry rides the ring at the ramp angle\n\nA Circular with entry Ramp (no user ramp angle) posted the legacy chord:\na ring returns to its own start, so every level change was a straight\nfeed down at the cutting feed, and an inner ring's first entry was a\n76 deg chord. Neither carried a note.\n\nOn the circular kernel (ring_zig) the Ramp arm now plans the zig-zag\nalong the ring at the ramp angle (3 deg default), as the helix's\nstand-down does. A ring too short for it dives at the plunge feed, named.\n\nPinned by circular_ramp_angle (red on upstream main).\n\nFixes #1609\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
